{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And these shall be to you for a statute of judgment throughout your generations in all your dwellings.</b> To teach that there shall be a Sanhedrin outside the Land so long as it functions in the Land — thus Rashi, of blessed memory, explained — unlike now, in the time of the Destruction, when it functions neither in the Land nor outside the Land. And the plain sense of the verse is: 'and these shall be to you for a statute of judgment' — that we should have a court judging even in this time, in matters of fines, and robbery, and wounds, and every monetary matter, and the obligation of lashes; and for this reason it says 'throughout your generations in all your dwellings.' But judgment in capital cases we do not have, for it is written in chapter four of the four modes of execution (Deuteronomy 17): ״ובאת אל הכהנים הלוים ואל השופט״ — when there is a kohen there is judgment; when there is no kohen there is no judgment. And so they taught in the Mekhilta: from where do we know that they put to death only before the House [Temple]? For it is stated (Exodus 21): ״מעם מזבחי תקחנו למות״ — if there is a House you put to death, and if not, you do not put to death."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:01.616092933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}